{
    "background_story": "Malcolm was a former army medic who had seen his fair share of battles. During his tours in the Middle East, he witnessed firsthand the devastating effects of antipersonnel mines on civilians. The memories of maimed children and innocent bystanders haunted him long after he left the service. Upon his return to the States, Malcolm dedicated his life to raising awareness about the dangers of these indiscriminate weapons. He became a vocal advocate for banning antipersonnel mines worldwide, working closely with international organizations to push for policy changes. Malcolm's tireless efforts eventually led to the establishment of a non-profit organization that specialized in mine removal and victim rehabilitation. His work was a testament to the human cost of war and the importance of protecting civilians from the ravages of conflict.",
